# concept Retrieval-augmented generation {#retrieval_augmented_generation}

Generation conditioned on documents retrieved from an external corpus in addition to parametric model state.

# claim Retrieval and model memory are distinct knowledge channels {#claim_two_channels}

Evidence: `{#source_rag}` and `{#claim_retrieval_context}`. Retrieved context can be inspected and changed without retraining model weights. Confidence: high for the architectural distinction.

# openquestion Citation fidelity {#question_citation_fidelity}

Under what conditions does a generated answer faithfully reflect the retrieved evidence rather than merely cite it? Requires answer-level evaluation; retrieval alone does not resolve it.

# relates wiki/transformers

Transformer language models are commonly used as the parametric generator.
